Description: stop the FTP receiver thread cooperatively instead of kill_thread
 The destructor called kill_thread() on the receiver thread, which on
 V\OS kills the whole team instead of one thread. Disconnect() has
 already closed the control socket and raised fAbort before that point,
 so the receiver loop exits by itself: resume the thread first (it is
 only resumed by Connect() on the normal path, and wait_for_thread()
 would hang on a never-started thread) and then wait for it.
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/FtpPositive
--- a/src/FTPClient.cpp
+++ b/src/FTPClient.cpp
@@ -51,7 +52,14 @@
 TFTPClient::~TFTPClient()
 {
 	this->Disconnect();
-	if (fReceiverThreadID >= B_OK) kill_thread(fReceiverThreadID);
+	// No kill_thread(): it takes the whole team with it on VOS.
+	// Disconnect() has already raised fAbort and closed the socket, so
+	// the receiver loop exits by itself; resume first in case the thread
+	// was never started (Connect() does the normal resume).
+	if (fReceiverThreadID >= B_OK) {
+		resume_thread(fReceiverThreadID);
+		wait_for_thread(fReceiverThreadID, NULL);
+	}
 	delete fReplyBuff;
 	if (fSemID >= B_OK) delete_sem(fSemID);
 }
